From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jokubas Maciulaitis <ubitas52@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 17:52:36 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] mtd: blkdevs: create block devices on gluebi volumes
 again

UBI volumes that gluebi exposes as MTD devices get no mtdblock device
since mtd_blkdevs started skipping MTD_UBIVOLUME; ubiblock is the way
mainline offers. Boot loaders that already pass root=/dev/mtdblockN for
a squashfs in a gluebi volume, as on the Onkyo receivers, then cannot
boot this kernel at all. Give gluebi volumes their block devices again;
they are read-only users of a static volume.
---
 drivers/mtd/mtd_blkdevs.c | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/mtd/mtd_blkdevs.c b/drivers/mtd/mtd_blkdevs.c
index 28e09d080..472d6f4fb 100644
--- a/drivers/mtd/mtd_blkdevs.c
+++ b/drivers/mtd/mtd_blkdevs.c
@@ -457,7 +457,7 @@ static void blktrans_notify_add(struct mtd_info *mtd)
 {
 	struct mtd_blktrans_ops *tr;
 
-	if (mtd->type == MTD_ABSENT || mtd->type == MTD_UBIVOLUME)
+	if (mtd->type == MTD_ABSENT)
 		return;
 
 	list_for_each_entry(tr, &blktrans_majors, list)
@@ -497,7 +497,7 @@ int register_mtd_blktrans(struct mtd_blktrans_ops *tr)
 	mutex_lock(&mtd_table_mutex);
 	list_add(&tr->list, &blktrans_majors);
 	mtd_for_each_device(mtd)
-		if (mtd->type != MTD_ABSENT && mtd->type != MTD_UBIVOLUME)
+		if (mtd->type != MTD_ABSENT)
 			tr->add_mtd(tr, mtd);
 	mutex_unlock(&mtd_table_mutex);
 	return 0;
